<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">László Rajk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1909–1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">László Rajk was a Hungarian communist who served as minister of the interior from 1946 to 1948 and then as foreign minister. In 1949 he was arrested, accused of spying for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josip-broz-tito">Tito</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> and the West, and condemned in a show trial organised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matyas-rakosi">Mátyás Rákosi</a>; he was executed in October 1949. His reburial in October 1956 helped spark the Hungarian Revolution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/laszlo-rajk.jpg" alt="László Rajk" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kommunizmuskutató Intézet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rajk_Laszlo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
